  "construction": "Reversing fold of a pair-partition CPM CSS code of arXiv:2609.30069 with J = 3, L = 10, P = 24. Parent qubit q = c*P + t. Parent X row (j,s) meets c*P + ((s - E[j][c]) mod P) for each block c. The involution is pi(c*P + t) = sigma[c]*P + ((-t - B[sigma[c]]) mod P). Folded site i pairs the i-th smallest q with q < pi(q) with pi(q). Each parent X row becomes one generator, X where it meets a representative and Z where it meets a partner. E = [[21, 12, 23, 10, 6, 15, 3, 19, 6, 5], [14, 21, 23, 6, 13, 12, 7, 8, 0, 6], [4, 1, 8, 18, 2, 18, 4, 11, 0, 16]], sigma = [9, 6, 8, 4, 3, 7, 1, 5, 2, 0], B = [21, 0, 10, 23, 23, 1, 0, 1, 10, 21].",
